<title>FRANCE: Bull Q1 sales dip, sees Q2 rise.</title>
<headline>Bull Q1 sales dip, sees Q2 rise.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-05-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>First three months of 1997</p>
<p>(All figures in millions of French francs)</p>
<p>    Turnover				  4,366    vs    4,566</p>
<p>NOTE - Cie des Machines Bull said in a statement the sales drop versus the same time last year was due to rationalisation of its personal computer distribution business, where sales were down 207 million. Failure to do better than flat sales in the other areas was due to the generally gloomy market climate in European and especially in France, it said.</p>
<p>The group expected second quarter sales to rise and noted that in April sales rose nine percent.</p>
<p>-- Paris Newsroom +33 1 4221 5452</p>
